{"id":"geres-moto","title":"Gerês by motorcycle: a weekend loop from Porto","who":"Classic route · Portugal's only national park","when":"All year (spring and autumn best)","vehicle":"Motorcycle, 2–3 days","kind":"moto","color":"#166534","summary":"A weekend from Porto into the Peneda-Gerês National Park: tight mountain roads with hairpins, granite villages with stone granaries at Soajo and Lindoso, the Portela do Homem pass on the Spanish border, the drowned village of Vilarinho das Furnas, waterfalls, wild garranos and long lunches. Narrow roads: ride gently.","sources":[{"label":"MyRoute: round trip from Gerês (September 2025)","url":"https://www.myrouteapp.com/motor-and-car-routes/pt/1763016/Round-trip-from-Geres"},{"label":"VisitPortugal: um passeio pelo Gerês","url":"https://www.visitportugal.com/pt-pt/content/um-passeio-pelo-geres"}],"approximate":"A common loop; the roads are the router's choice.","km":238,"bbox":[-8.6103,41.1502,-8.1085,42.0626],"stops":[{"name":"Porto","place":"Porto, Portugal","at":[41.1502,-8.6103],"text":"Out north on the A3 or the old N14.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Puente_Don_Luis_I%2C_Oporto%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_13.JPG/500px-Puente_Don_Luis_I%2C_Oporto%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_13.JPG","page":"Porto","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Puente_Don_Luis_I%2C_Oporto%2C_Portugal%2C_2012-05-09%2C_DD_13.JPG","credit":"Diego Delso","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Braga","place":"Braga, Portugal","at":[41.5511,-8.428],"text":"The baroque stairs of Bom Jesus.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Treppenaufgang_Bom_Jesus_do_Monte.jpg/500px-Treppenaufgang_Bom_Jesus_do_Monte.jpg","page":"Sanctuary of Bom Jesus do Monte","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Treppenaufgang_Bom_Jesus_do_Monte.jpg","credit":"Botafogo","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Gerês (vila)","place":"Caldas do Gerês","at":[41.7274,-8.1631],"